<p>During development, I often encounter a <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">UIButton</code> whose tap area is too small, but I don’t want to change the button’s size.</p>

<p>Today’s article shares the code that solves this problem.</p>

<h1 id="implementation-approach">Implementation Approach</h1>

<ul>
  <li>Subclass UIButton and override its <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">hitTest:</code> method</li>
  <li>Subclass UIButton and override the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">point:inside:withEvent:</code> method</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="the-first-approach">The First Approach</h2>

<div class="language-swift highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><table class="rouge-table"><tbody><tr><!-- <td class="rouge-gutter gl"><pre class="lineno">1
